,"headline":"45…Rxc7!! A real sacrifice: Black gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the rook on c7 where it can be taken.","White can take, but after 46.Rxc7 Rh3 47.Kg1 Ne2+ the engine rates it 0.00.","Takes the pawn on c7.","45…Rxc7 stops c8=Q+.","White was threatening c8=Q+, promoting to a queen. Rxc7 takes care of it.","Takes the c7 pawn."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"45…Rxc7!! gives up the rook on c7 to stay in the game: after it Black holds the balance (0.00); anything else leaves Black losing (+6.38)."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"45…Rxc7 puts the rook on c7 where it can be taken by the rook on c1. That's a whole rook on offer."},{"title":"If White takes the rook","text":"46.Rxc7 is met by 46…Rh3, threatening …Rh1# and mate. Then 47…Rh1+ gives check, and 48…Rh2+ gives check. Black is a piece and a pawn down: Black holds the balance (0.00). This is White's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 45…Ra8, is clearly weaker (+6.38 against 0.00). White answers 46.c8=Q+. That would leave Black losing."}]},{"ply":100,"name":"50…Ra1","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"50…Ra1! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Attacks the a5 pawn, which is undefended.","The rook takes the half-open a-file.","The next best move, 50…Rb2+, would drop Black's winning chances from 47% to 23% (+3.35).","50…Ra1 takes the half-open a-file and attacks the a5 pawn, which is undefended.","White answers 51.Ra7.","Engine line: 51.Ra7 Nd5 52.Ra8+ Kh7 53.Bc5 e4 (+0.07)."]}],"opening":{"name":"Italian Game: Giuoco Pianissimo, Normal","eco":"C50","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 10…Qe7: 20 moves in all, 10 by White and 10 by Black.","Theory runs out after 10…Qe7: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}